==Irish==

===Etymology===
From a conflation of {{inh|ga|sga|sár|g=m||chief, ruler}} and {{der|ga|en|tsar}}, {{der|ga|ru|царь}}, from {{der|ga|orv|цьсарь}}, from {{der|ga|cu|цѣсарь}}, from {{der|ga|got|𐌺𐌰𐌹𐍃𐌰𐍂||emperor}}, from {{der|ga|la|Caesar}}. The Old Irish may be [[elliptical]] for some such compound like (modern) {{m|ga|[[sár-|sár]][[fear|fhear]]}}

===Noun===
{{ga-noun|g=m|sáir|sáir}}

# [[tsar]]
# {{lb|ga|literary}} [[overlord]], [[ruler]]

====Declension====
{{ga-decl-m1|sá|r|ir}}

====Derived terms====
